[[File:Charli XCX (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright|The guest appearance of [[Charli XCX]] on "Fancy" was received well by critics.]]
"Fancy" received overall positive reception from [[music journalism|music critics]]. Brad Stern of ''[[MTV Buzzworthy]]'' remarked, "Not since [[Fergie (singer)|Fergie]]'s '[[Glamorous (Fergie song)|Glamorous]]' has there been such a spectacularly sass-filled ode to the glam life," praising their chemistry, calling it "a match made in heaven that we never would've expected."<ref name="mtvbuzz">{{cite web|url=http://buzzworthy.mtv.com/2012/02/07/iggy-azalea-fancy-charli-xcx/ |title=Iggy Azalea Gets Aggressively 'Fancy' On Her New Charli XCX Collaboration |publisher=MTV Buzzworthy |date=7 February 2014 |access-date=26 February 2014}}{{dead link|date=June 2024|bot=medic}}{{cbignore|bot=medic}}</ref> Chris Tomas of ''Hip Hop Wired'' wrote that the song "could be the hit record Iggy Azalea has been looking for," noting that "Charli XCX also provides a very potent chorus that women will be chanting in their clubs, cars, and the like."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://hiphopwired.com/2014/02/07/iggy-azalea-ft-charli-xcx-fancy-listen/ |title=Iggy Azalea ft. Charli XCX – "Fancy" [Listen] |publisher=Hip-Hop Wired |date=7 February 2014 |access-date=7 February 2014}}</ref> Mike Wass of ''[[Idolator (website)|Idolator]]'' claimed the track is "the duet we've all been waiting for" and "a swag-drenched hip hop/pop delight."<ref>{{cite web |last=Wass |first=Mike |url=http://www.idolator.com/7504760/iggy-azalea-charli-xcx-fancy-listen |archive-url=https://archive.today/20140303212903/http://www.idolator.com/7504760/iggy-azalea-charli-xcx-fancy-listen |url-status=dead |archive-date=3 March 2014 |title=Iggy Azalea's Charli XCX-Assisted Single "Fancy" Arrives: Listen |publisher=Idolator. SpinMedia |date=6 February 2014 |access-date=7 February 2014 }}</ref> Janice Llamoca of ''Hip Hop DX'' defined it as "a hip hop-slash-pop party anthem in which the emcee lyrically displays her confidence."<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/singles/id.26599/title.Iggy+Azalea+f.+Charli+XCX-Fancy |title=Iggy Azalea f. Charli XCX - Fancy |publisher=HipHop DX |date=7 February 2014 |access-date=7 February 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141006142507/http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/singles/id.26599/title.Iggy+Azalea+f.+Charli+XCX-Fancy |archive-date=6 October 2014 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

Joe Gross of ''[[Rolling Stone]]'' gave the song a mixed score of 3 out of 5 stars, writing that Azalea "deftly handles the ratchet beat while Charli XCX's earworm hook holds it all down," writing that the song "[doesn't] bring '88 back [but] they can swing on chandeliers with the best of them".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/songreviews/fancy-20140221 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140306195208/http://www.rollingstone.com/music/songreviews/fancy-20140221 |url-status=dead |archive-date=6 March 2014 |title=Iggy Azalea feat. Charli XCX Fancy Song Review |publisher=[[Rolling Stone]]. Wenner Media |date=21 February 2014 |access-date=3 April 2014}}</ref> Jamie Parmenter of ''Renowned for Sound'' noted that the song showed the influence of [[Missy Elliott]], and that "Iggy is almost playing a character or parody of herself like [[Eminem]] is renowned for," praising Charli XCX for "nicely breaking up the song, sounding like an edgy [[Gwen Stefani]], matching with Iggy's rebel style."<ref name=renowned>{{cite news|last=Parmenter|first=Jamie|title=Single Review: Iggy Azalea – 'Fancy' (feat. Charli XCX)|url=http://renownedforsound.com/index.php/single-review-iggy-azalea-feat-charli-xcx-fancy/|access-date=10 May 2014|newspaper=Renowned for Sound|date=19 March 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140512220906/http://renownedforsound.com/index.php/single-review-iggy-azalea-feat-charli-xcx-fancy/|archive-date=12 May 2014|url-status=dead}}</ref> Bill Lamb of ''[[About.com]]'', like Jake Gross, gave a mixed response, but echoed the same thought as Parmenter, praising "Charli XCX's Gwen Stefani styled vocals on the chorus" and noting that its lyrics has been done even better by Stefani nearly 10 years ago on '[[Luxurious]]'." However, Lamb also stated that the entire song seemed "a bit too recycled" and had a "tiresome obsession with material culture delivered with a straight face."<ref name="about.com">{{cite web|last=Lamb|first=Bill|title=Review: Iggy Azalea "Fancy" featuring Charli XCX|url=http://top40.about.com/od/2014Reviews/fl/Review-Iggy-Azalea-Fancy-featuring-Charli-XCX.htm|work=[[About.com]]|access-date=10 May 2014|archive-date=14 October 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141014141333/http://top40.about.com/od/2014Reviews/fl/Review-Iggy-Azalea-Fancy-featuring-Charli-XCX.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref> The track was placed at number nineteen on ''Rolling Stones'''s 50 Best Songs of 2014 list.<ref>{{cite web|title=50 Best Songs of 2014|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/lists/50-best-songs-of-2014-20141203/iggy-azalea-feat-charli-xcx-fancy-20141202|work=rollingstone.com|date=3 December 2014 |access-date=4 December 2014}}</ref> It was named [[iTunes]]' best song of 2014 on [[Apple Inc.|Apple]]'s annual Best-Ofs.<ref>{{cite web|title=Pharrell and 'Frozen' Top iTunes' Year-End List, Beyonce Named Best Artist|url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/6385969/itunes-year-end-sales-chart-list-pharrell-frozen-beyonce|work=billboard.com|access-date=8 December 2014}}</ref> "Fancy" was also placed at number one on [[MTV]]'s Best Songs of 2014.<ref>{{cite web|title=Best Songs of 2014 - MTV|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/2018061/best-songs-2014/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141224035948/http://www.mtv.com/news/2018061/best-songs-2014/|url-status=dead|archive-date=24 December 2014|work=mtv.com|access-date=10 December 2014}}</ref> ''[[The Village Voice]]''{{'}}s [[Pazz & Jop]] annual critics' poll listed "Fancy" at number 26 on their poll for the best music of 2014, along with [[Ariana Grande]]'s "[[Problem (Ariana Grande song)|Problem]]", on which Azalea was featured.{{citation needed|date=October 2019}}

